      "side": 1,
      "message": "I apologize for being quite slow with code review.  I may need to take a day off on Friday, but I hope to be able to carve out most of Monday to finish reviewing this CL.  Let me send out (shamefully small) a few pieces of feedback below.\n\nOne high-level question that I had was whether incremental/streaming decoding is a requirement or not (i.e. being able to resume decoding after receiving more input bytes, without having to start from scratch).  Do we know for a fact if one or both `third_party/blink/renderer/platform/image-decoders/bmp/bmp_image_reader.cc` and `third_party/skia/src/codec/SkBmpCodec.cpp` don\u0027t support streaming decoding (and therefore we can use this as a justification to avoid implementing streaming decoding in the new codec)?\n\nI also wanted to give a quick disclaimer that I think we\u0027re not 100% sure where exactly this code should land.  IIRC in the last sync-up meeting we discussed that developing new code in Skia may be easier than splitting the implementation into separate Skia and crates.io-crate parts.  At the same time, we probably should discuss the long-term home and ownership of this code (especially since landing CLs such as this one in Skia kind of implicitly makes Skia the owners of this code).  This doesn\u0027t necessarily reviewing and iterating on this code, but I wanted to be upfront about it - I hope that we can hash it out next week during our sync-up meeting.",
      "revId": "e33faf05ba40ab0f1496c3ce8c498d3e5c5672d4",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
